    "#### How to read this plot:\n",
    "\n",
    "The **salmon/red dots clustered in the middle** are the 20 course activities — notice a few of them\n",
    "are noticeably bigger than the rest. Those are the \"hub\" activities that huge numbers of students\n",
    "interact with (very likely early, mandatory items like an intro video or a welcome quiz that\n",
    "everyone has to click through). The **blue dots** are the 78 students, mostly smaller and scattered\n",
    "around the edges, each connected to just a few activities.\n",
    "\n",
    "**This picture visually confirms two things we calculated above:**\n",
    "\n",
    "(1) the graph is one single connected mass with no isolated blue or red dots floating off on their own, matching `Is connected: True`, and\n",
    "\n",
    "(2) a small number of shared hub activities is what keeps everyone within a short number of hops of\n",
    "each other, which is exactly why the diameter came out as small as 5 even with 98 total nodes."
   ]
